    {
      "metin": "* In Egypt, the name of the fish is said to come from Coptic ⲫⲟⲣⲓ (phori, “Mugil cephalus”) – in Bohairic, also ϥⲟⲣⲓ (fori), while in Sahidic it is ⲃⲱⲣⲉ (bōre); however, the name is also used in Morocco and Lebanon, and the relation with Japanese 鰡 / 鯔 (bora) denoting the same species of fish remains enigmatic.\n* The meaning of a fatty bread is from Hindustani (Hindi पूरी (pūrī) / Urdu پُورِی (pūrī)).\n* The sense of a pipe and the sense of a vehicle’s horn is from Ottoman Turkish بورو (boru, “duct, pipe, tube; horn”). Doublet of بُرْغِيّ (burḡiyy, “screw”).",
